The legacy disposition code set had four closing values. C-1 closed with no=
 deficiencies, C-2 closed no further action, C-3 referred, and C-4 closed o=
n registrant undertaking. SENTRY's code set has three. There is no C-4.<br =
/>
<br />
Your answer on the call was that C-4 records were mapped to C-2 because bot=
h are non-referral closures. I understand why that is the obvious mapping a=
nd I want to flag what it costs. C-4 exists precisely to say that the regis=
trant promised the staff something in writing and that the promise is open =
for verification at the next examination. C-2 says only that the staff foun=
d nothing worth following up. Mapping C-4 onto it does not lose a label, it=
 deletes the one fact the next examiner needs, and it does so on exactly th=
e examinations whose correspondence also did not migrate. After the migrati=
on there is no field in SENTRY and no document in SENTRY that would tell an=
 examiner an undertaking exists.<br />
<br />
Can we get C-4 restored as a distinct value, or at minimum a flag on the mi=
grated records?<br />
